    "civilRightsImpact": "The registration duty falls on the person themself, and the definition contains no citizen or LPR exemption: a U.S. citizen or green-card holder who acts as a covered agent of a PRC-linked principal — acting at its direction, financed by it, and engaging in political activity — would have had to register or face penalties, a burden on civic participation tied to status-linked activity, hence Tier 1. The reach is conduct-gated (all three requirements together), not triggered by party membership alone. Covered origins: the PRC as named — mainland China, Hong Kong, and Macau. Taiwan (the ROC) is not the PRC as named and is not covered. U.S. citizens are covered where they act as covered agents — the text contains no citizen exemption.",
