    "session": "57th Legislature, Second Regular Session (2026)",
    "category": "property",
    "target": "A foreign adversary nation or a “foreign adversary agent” acquiring a substantial interest (15% threshold) in Arizona real property. Section 33-443(N)(7)(f) defines “foreign adversary agent” to incorporate “a foreign person as defined in 31 CFR 802.221 when applied to a foreign adversary nation” — and 31 CFR 802.221/802.220 define “foreign person”/“foreign national” as any individual other than a U.S. national, with no actual agency relationship required.",
    "restrictions": "Property restrictions (15% substantial-interest threshold)",
    "penalties": "Class 5 felony for the related equipment prohibition; divestiture machinery",
    "summary": "Section 33-443(A) bars a foreign adversary nation or foreign adversary agent from acquiring a substantial interest in Arizona real property. The critical move is definitional: §33-443(N)(7)(f) folds the federal “foreign person” definition (31 CFR 802.221) into “foreign adversary agent,” and that federal definition covers any individual other than a U.S. national (31 CFR 802.220). The bill’s title says “agent,” but subparagraph (f) reaches lawful permanent residents and visa holders by immigration status alone — no order, direction, control, or agency relationship with a foreign government is required. A “foreign adversary nation” is a country the Director of National Intelligence identifies as a national-security risk in each of the three most recent annual threat assessments; the PRC is named throughout.",
    "civilRightsImpact": "This is the tracker’s calibration case for definition-stretching: the operative bar reaches Chinese LPRs and Chinese students and workers on visas — people with no connection to any foreign government — because (f) deems every non-U.S.-national an “agent.” That is a nationality-and-status-based property ban on community members, hence Tier 1. Covered origins: mainland China, Hong Kong, and Macau (the PRC as assessed). Taiwan is not identified as a foreign adversary nation and is not covered. U.S. citizens are U.S. nationals and are expressly outside the incorporated definition — citizens are NOT covered, a point the record states plainly rather than leaving to inference.",
